Scenario: Generate new DXP and Commerce Production non aggregate and non combined aggregate licenses using different end dates
	Testing the ability to generate non aggregate licenses for two separate DXP and Commerce products as well as a combined aggregate for both products for a T4 DXP project from koroneiki on provisioning

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORLICKORLIC                         |
	| Contact Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | lic.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static start and end dates
	And I generate future static full start and end dates
	And I generate future static yyyymmdd start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Commerce Subscription Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 0 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" for "Commerce Subscription Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I go to the license index page
	And I click on the generate license button on the license index
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Account | Select Entity | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	| Version | Select        | 7.2                           | |
	| Type    | Select        | DXP Production (Production)   | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Name          | Input    | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name        | |
	| Description   | Input    | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Description | |
	| Host Name     | Input    | localhost                                          | |
	| IP Addresses  | Textarea | 123.45.67.89                                       | |
	| MAC Addresses | Textarea | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F                                  | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | DXP Production                | |
	And I obtain the license key ID value from the license details page
	And I rename the first license key ID variable
	When I go to the license index page
	And I click on the generate license button on the license index
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Account         | Select Entity | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}                 | |
	| Product         | Select        | Commerce Subscription Production              | |
	| Version         | Select        | 1                                             | |
	| Type            | Select        | Commerce Subscription Production (Production) | |
	| Expiration Date | Input         | ${staticYyyyMmDdFutureOriginalEndDate}        | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Name          | Input    | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Name        | |
	| Description   | Input    | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Description | |
	| Host Name     | Input    | localhost                                          | |
	| IP Addresses  | Textarea | 123.45.67.89                                       | |
	| MAC Addresses | Textarea | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F                                  | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Korlic - ${staticProjectName}    | |
	| Product | Commerce Subscription Production | |
	And I obtain the license key ID value from the license details page
	And I rename the second license key ID variable
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korlic"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korlic - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Licenses" tab
	And I select the following licenses under the licenses tab
	| Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name |
	| Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Name |
	And I click on the "Download" button in the dropdown menu for all licenses under the license tab
	Then I should be able to view the license with the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name" and the following values on the download license page
	| Name        | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Name        |
	| Description | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License1 Description |
	| Version     | 7.2                                                |
	| Product     | DXP Production                                     |
	| Type        | DXP Production (Production)                        |
	| Status      | ACTIVE                                             |
	And I should be able to view the license with the keyword "Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Name" and the following values on the download license page
	| Name        | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Name        |
	| Description | Korlic - ${staticProjectName} License2 Description |
	| Product     | Commerce Subscription Production                   |
	| Type        | Commerce Subscription Production (Production)      |
	| Status      | ACTIVE                                             |
	And I should be able to view the download button for the following license key id values on the download license page
	| ${staticLicenseKeyId2} |
	And I should be able to view the download button for the following license key id values on the download license page
	| ${staticLicenseKeyId1} |
	And I should not be able to view the download button for the following license key id values on the download license page
	| ${staticLicenseKeyId2} |
	| ${staticLicenseKeyId1} |

Scenario: Generate new DXP and Commerce Production non aggregate and non combined aggregate licenses using different start dates
	Testing the ability to generate non aggregate licenses for two separate DXP and Commerce products as well as a combined aggregate for both products for a T4 DXP project from koroneiki on provisioning

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
